  "question": {
    "text": "If the integral <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#921;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msup><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp; is the constant of integration and <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the value of&nbsp;<math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
